.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-6.log:10827:./SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:504:| `ledger_entry_rejected` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `signal` (str — fixed vocabulary of ONE: `ledger_write_gate`; this action has exactly one producer, so any other value names a caller that is not the gate and is COERCED), `decision` (str — CLOSED enum: `accept` / `reject`; an unreadable value COERCES to `reject`, FAIL-CLOSED, because an unreadable security verdict is a rejection and never an acceptance), `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `not_scanned_trusted_provenance` / `scanner_hit` / `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input`; off-enum COERCES to `malformed_input`, also fail-CLOSED), `family` (str — CLOSED enum, the UNION of the gate's own local families {`none`, `scanner_unavailable`, `oversize`, `malformed_input`, `unknown_family`} and the pattern CATALOGUE `_lib/injection_patterns.family_names()` {`directive_prose`, `harness_mimicry`, `provider_tokens`, `role_preamble`}; off-enum COERCED to `unknown_family`. Deliberately STRICTER than `prompt_injection_detected`, whose branch allowlists `family` by NAME but leaves its VALUE caller-chosen), `hits_count` (int 0..9999 — clamped), `bytes_scanned` (int 0..8192 — clamped at the gate's `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES`; an oversize body is rejected WITHOUT scanning, so this ceiling can never truncate a legitimate value), `scanned` (int 0/1), `enforced` (int 0/1 — whether the fail-CLOSED verdict BINDS in the current posture; kept separate from `decision` so an advisory-window row records what enforcement WOULD have done without pretending it happened), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W4 / ADR-195 — the ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), registered by Owner decision 2026-08-25 ("3 actions"). It exists precisely so a discard is NOT filed as `prompt_injection_detected`: routing `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input` into a DETECTION action would poison the very false-positive series the advisory window has to measure. There is deliberately NO fallback action — a missing or raising emitter degrades to a LOUD breadcrumb and `audit_channel="unavailable"`, never to a quieter series. Typed emitter `emit_ledger_entry_rejected` (keywords mirror `GateVerdict.to_audit_fields()` exactly). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the rejected entry BODY (not even a truncated preview — public repo, LLM06), the entry id, and any path. NO ATLAS technique (the DETECTION that may underlie a `scanner_hit` is `prompt_injection_detected`'s job; this row is the gate's disposal record). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-6.log:10828:./SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:590:| v2.59 | PLAN-179 W2 + W4 (staged-w24 pack, ADR-195 work-boundary persistence; Owner decision 2026-08-25 "3 actions — registra ledger_entry_rejected") — 3 NEW metadata-only actions. `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` + `ledger_checkpoint_skipped`: the ADVISORY work-boundary rail (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash) makes an OMITTED plan checkpoint visible at the one boundary this repo already has — a commit — instead of at session death, which S309 proved does not arrive. The two are separate actions so the measure-first window has a denominator. `ledger_entry_rejected`: the W4 ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), which used to borrow `prompt_injection_detected` for `reason="scanner_hit"` and go breadcrumb-only for the other four reasons; that fallback rung is REMOVED with this registration, because filing an infrastructure discard as a DETECTION poisons the FPR series the window measures. All three route through dedicated deny-by-default `_scrub_*` branches (`_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`), NONE is in `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`, and every integer field is TYPE-strict (`bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, `float` -> `0`, never rounded — S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). The commit message, the committed paths, the ledger content and the rejected entry body have no allowed field name at all. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327 -> 330. ONE new typed emitter (`emit_ledger_entry_rejected`). HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(3 new per-action allowlists + closed enums `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_OUTCOMES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIP_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SCOPE_SOURCES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_STATE_KINDS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_DECISIONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` + the TYPE-strict clamp `_ledger_int_field` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
