.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2359:+| `context_pressure_observed` (v2.56) | `action`, `used_bucket` (int — CLOSED set of PERCENT rungs: `40` / `60` / `80` / `90` / `95`; the unit lives in the field NAME. The check `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected (it is an `int` subclass, so `True` would otherwise sail through any numeric test) and `float` is rejected even when it COMPARES equal to a rung (`40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python), because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event, leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — the same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`. Anything off-set is COERCED to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a coerced one), `event_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `precompact` / `sessionstart_compact` / `userpromptsubmit` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed. Only `precompact` has a shipped producer in the PLAN-179 W0/W1 bundle; `sessionstart_compact` — the channel PLAN-179 debate amendment 8.1 designates PRIMARY — and `userpromptsubmit` are RESERVED, and a consumer MUST read their absence as “no producer yet”, NEVER as “no pressure observed on that channel”. The PostCompact `additionalContext` channel stays UNPROVEN until the PLAN-179 W0-1 probe lands and is therefore deliberately ABSENT from the enum), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`), `session_id` (present ONLY when the producer holds a session id derived from the HOOK INPUT; deliberately OMITTED otherwise rather than filled from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, which an agent can set — an unattributed row is honest, a wrongly-attributed one is not; PLAN-179 amendment r1-C1), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W0 US2 / debate amendment 8.1 (ADR-153 continuity successor rail, 2026-08-18) — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2361:+| `salt_rotation_registered` (v2.58) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum {`first_mint`, `migration_mint`, `other`}; anything else COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `salt_scope` (str — fixed vocabulary of one: `project`, the ADR-079 S318 salt unit; anything else COERCED), `slug_sha256` (str — 16-hex sha256 PREFIX of the native project slug; shape-checked, malformed COERCED to the sentinel `"invalid"`, never echoed), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-182 W1 — the ONE sanctioned, REGISTERED salt-rotation event (ADR-079 S318 amendment §2: minting a per-project `.salt` is observable in the chain, never silent; the pre-S318 `get_instance_salt()` minted with no error, no log, no signal). Producer: `_lib/injection_salt.py::_register_mint` via LAZY `emit_generic` at mint time only (no module-load coupling; a `salt-minted.json` sidecar next to the salt is the forensic ground truth when the emit path is unavailable). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_SALT_ROTATION_REGISTERED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the slug TEXT as a payload value (only its 16-hex `slug_sha256` prefix travels), the salt bytes, and the salt's own path. This clause governs PAYLOAD values only: the baseline `project` field listed above carries the repository path, as it does on every registered action and as it did in v1.3.0 — it is a required base field of the envelope, not a payload value, and removing it would leave the line without attribution. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2364:+| `ledger_entry_rejected` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `signal` (str — fixed vocabulary of ONE: `ledger_write_gate`; this action has exactly one producer, so any other value names a caller that is not the gate and is COERCED), `decision` (str — CLOSED enum: `accept` / `reject`; an unreadable value COERCES to `reject`, FAIL-CLOSED, because an unreadable security verdict is a rejection and never an acceptance), `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `not_scanned_trusted_provenance` / `scanner_hit` / `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input`; off-enum COERCES to `malformed_input`, also fail-CLOSED), `family` (str — CLOSED enum, the UNION of the gate's own local families {`none`, `scanner_unavailable`, `oversize`, `malformed_input`, `unknown_family`} and the pattern CATALOGUE `_lib/injection_patterns.family_names()` {`directive_prose`, `harness_mimicry`, `provider_tokens`, `role_preamble`}; off-enum COERCED to `unknown_family`. Deliberately STRICTER than `prompt_injection_detected`, whose branch allowlists `family` by NAME but leaves its VALUE caller-chosen), `hits_count` (int 0..9999 — clamped), `bytes_scanned` (int 0..8192 — clamped at the gate's `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES`; an oversize body is rejected WITHOUT scanning, so this ceiling can never truncate a legitimate value), `scanned` (int 0/1), `enforced` (int 0/1 — whether the fail-CLOSED verdict BINDS in the current posture; kept separate from `decision` so an advisory-window row records what enforcement WOULD have done without pretending it happened), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W4 / ADR-195 — the ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), registered by Owner decision 2026-08-25 ("3 actions"). It exists precisely so a discard is NOT filed as `prompt_injection_detected`: routing `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input` into a DETECTION action would poison the very false-positive series the advisory window has to measure. There is deliberately NO fallback action — a missing or raising emitter degrades to a LOUD breadcrumb and `audit_channel="unavailable"`, never to a quieter series. Typed emitter `emit_ledger_entry_rejected` (keywords mirror `GateVerdict.to_audit_fields()` exactly). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the rejected entry BODY (not even a truncated preview — public repo, LLM06), the entry id, and any path. NO ATLAS technique (the DETECTION that may underlie a `scanner_hit` is `prompt_injection_detected`'s job; this row is the gate's disposal record). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2365:+| `session_memory_delta_observed` (v2.60) | `action`, `session_id` (str — threaded from the harness event, clamped ≤128, no silent default), `project` (str — `str(repo_root)`, clamped ≤256, the same field every event on this rail already carries), `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum `written` · `absent` · `index_only` · `start_unknown` · `dir_missing` · `not_writable` · `error` · `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, NEVER to `written` — an unparseable observation must never be laundered into a healthy-class value), `files_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries in the native memory dir), `modified_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries whose `st_mtime` falls inside THIS session's window — a WINDOW-scoped observation over the SHARED per-project dir: a CONCURRENT session's write inside the window counts (ADR-005 overlap is a supported case) and stat carries no author, so this is never an authorship claim), `index_modified` (bool — `MEMORY.md` specifically; non-bool coerced to `false`), `anchor_source` (str — CLOSED enum `chain` · `state_file` · `none`: which step of the session-start resolution answered — the HMAC chain's own `session_start` event via bounded scan (≤200 lines / ≤256 KiB / ≤100 ms; the OLDEST in-window match wins — a compact-restart re-emit for the same session id must not shrink the window — and a candidate is consumed only after its per-entry HMAC verifies against the previous line with the project key (verify-before-consume, ADR-160; `CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE=1` waives the integrity claim; scope is PER-ENTRY — the candidate against the ADJACENT line's declared digest, the predecessor itself NOT re-verified: a same-UID log writer reads the 0600 key and forges whole chains anyway (CLAUDE.md §5 boundary), so whole-chain integrity stays `verify_chain`'s offline job, never this bounded reader's claim); the chain is the anchor, never a mutable side file — the ADR-160 §3 / A6 principle), `state_file` — RETIRED in this same ceremony (rail r5: the record file is rewritten via `os.replace` on every tool update, which allocates a NEW inode and resets even `st_birthtime` — no immutable artifact exists on that surface); the enum value stays registered for wire-compat and is NEVER produced. Resolution is therefore chain-or-`none`, with REAL predecessor resolution on the chain leg (legacy `hmac:null` prefix lines are traversed to the last SIGNED line, mirroring `verify_chain`; genesis applies only when the bounded window covers the whole file), or the terminal `none` = "I do not know": the hook never substitutes "since midnight" or process start, because a wrong window produces a false `written`, worse than absent), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US8 (wave-179-close ceremony; implements the signed spec `PLAN-179/staged-w24/SESSIONEND-NOTE.md`) — SessionEnd memory-delta observation: ONE emit per session from `.claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py::decide`, immediately BEFORE the `session_end` emit so a reader scanning backwards from `session_end` finds it adjacent. STAT-ONLY producer: counts `st_mtime >= session_start` over the native memory dir and NEVER opens a memory file for write — memory writing stays a model/Owner decision; the count is window activity over the project dir, not per-session authorship (rail r6 P2-a); this action makes the OMISSION visible (`outcome=absent` is the case the historical `memory_writable` bit could not express; structural namespace activity — rename/delete, detected via the directory mtime inside the window — BLOCKS the absence class and the index_only exclusivity, because the closed enum cannot express a structural delta and `error` is the honest refusal — rail r17). A NEW action deliberately, not extra fields on `session_end`: overloading would conflate "the hook ran" with "a delta was observed" and change the meaning of an event with a landed row (v2.7). Typed producer `emit_session_memory_delta_observed` routes through the dedicated deny-by-default `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion + TYPE-strict int clamps (bool is an int subclass, and a float would drop the ENTIRE event at the canonical-json layer — both coerce to the sentinel 0, never rounded, never echoed), NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire, by name — the scrub operates on field NAMES (non-allowlisted keys are dropped; identity fields `session_id`/`project` are type-checked and clamped, their VALUES being the emitter-wide baseline contract every action shares — the typed wrapper is the sole sanctioned producer and `test_no_paths_on_the_wire` pins what it sends): the memory file names/basenames (rail r22: names travel on NO channel at all — five rail rounds of directive-smuggling bypasses proved free-form basenames unsanitizable for an instruction-adjacent surface, so the operator line is COUNTS-ONLY and the sanitized `names` list remains an internal gate for any future render; this supersedes the earlier "names to the operator" split of the W2 AC, deviation declared), the file bodies or any excerpt, the resolved memory-dir absolute path and the `$HOME`-derived slug, the raw `session_start` source line, any environment value. Kill-switch `CEO_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA` (unset = full; `quiet`/`1q` = event only, no operator line; `0`/`false`/`off`/`no` = nothing emitted — the `off` state needs NO gate-side waiver (rail r14, correcting the SESSIONEND-NOTE §104-108 model): the registered command remains a real hook, which the harness-config constant-emitter heuristic can never flag, and a substring allowlist entry would be inert for that purpose while opening an ADR-158 §2 bypass). Completeness residual (honest boundary, same as ADR-153 §H2): an ABSENT row is not evidence of an absent session — `CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0`, `disableAllHooks`, or a killed process all suppress it. Pre-registered DEATH criterion (SESSIONEND-NOTE.md §8): `outcome=absent` dominating a measurement window with no behaviour change means the rail is REMOVED, not kept as debt. NO ATLAS technique (governance/omission-visibility breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2376:+| v2.56 | PLAN-179 W0 US2 + W1 US3 + W1-b (context-continuity successor rail / ADR-153, debate amendments 8.1 + r1-C3, 2026-08-18) — 1 NEW metadata-only action `context_pressure_observed` (EDGE-TRIGGERED: emitted only on a percent-rung TRANSITION, gated by `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(...)` against the `context-pressure-last-bucket` marker under the gitignored `.claude/state/` — per-session when the producer supplies a session id (`<basename>.<sanitized-id>`), falling back to the bare project-wide basename otherwise, a documented degraded mode in which two concurrent sessions in one repo can interfere with each other's hysteresis; hysteresis, never sampling — a per-turn sampler would append one row per prompt while the session sits in one rung), PLUS 1 additive value on the EXISTING closed `snapshot_outcome` enum of `compaction_continuity_snapshot` — `written_session_scope`, the S309 fires-proof DOMINANT path where the snapshot lands in the session-scoped fallback because `resolve_plan_id()` could not name a plan — PLUS 1 NEW bounded field `constraint_count` on the EXISTING `compaction_context_reinjected` action. NO new typed emitter: `context_pressure_observed` goes through `emit_generic` (compaction-pair / `settings_tamper_detected` precedent) into a dedicated deny-by-default `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`; `plan_id` reuses the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator. **`used_bucket`'s integer typing is normative, not stylistic:** `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict (rejects `bool`, an `int` subclass, and rejects `float` — `40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python, so a plain membership test would wave a float onto the wire and `_lib/canonical_json.py` would then drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb; same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`). Off-set values coerce to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the `{40,60,80,90,95}` enum. **`pointer_count` is UNCHANGED** and keeps counting POINTERS ONLY — constraint pinning landed as the SEPARATE `constraint_count` rather than by re-defining what `pointer_count` measures, because a silently re-scoped counter makes its historical series uncomparable (amendment r1-C3 is what makes this SPEC bump non-optional). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. Registered via the PLAN-179 W0/W1 pack ceremony (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 324 -> 325; the staged set literal measures 325). **CODE/ROW PARITY — three integration gaps were found by the W0/W1 cross-file pass and are CLOSED by this same ceremony, so this row describes the wire as shipped, not as intended:** (1) `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch clamps it `max(0, min(99, int(...)))`, so the deny-by-default scrub keeps it; (2) the shipped producer of `context_pressure_observed` (`check_precompact_continuity.py:_progress_guard`) probes `getattr(audit_emit, "should_emit_context_pressure", None)` — the name that actually exists — and calls it with the crossed bucket, `state_dir = <project>/.claude/state` and the trusted session id, retrying the two-argument shape on `TypeError` so an adopter whose `audit_emit` predates per-session markers degrades to the project-wide marker instead of losing the observation; an earlier draft probed `edge_trigger_should_emit`, a name in neither library, which suppressed every emit; (3) that producer now sends the allowlisted trio `used_bucket` / `event_source` / `plan_id`, where `used_bucket` is the PERCENT rung from `_context_used_pct` + `_pressure_bucket` and the rung SET is DERIVED from `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` at call time rather than restated ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]); the earlier `used_tokens_bucket` (`used_tokens // 10000`) and `floor_tokens` are gone from the wire and survive only in the operator's stderr breadcrumb, which is the correct home for a raw count. A conformance test asserting this row against the wire is expected to pass. **Producer coverage is still partial and that is not a defect of this row:** `precompact` is the only `event_source` with a shipped producer; `sessionstart_compact` and `userpromptsubmit` remain RESERVED, and their absence means “no producer yet”, never “no pressure observed on that channel”. | *(1 additive value on the existing `_COMPACTION_SNAPSHOT_OUTCOMES` closed enum; 1 additive field on `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`; 1 new per-action allowlist `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` + closed sets `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` / `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCES` + type-strict validator `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` + edge-trigger helper `should_emit_context_pressure` and marker basename `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_STATE_BASENAME` in `audit_emit.py`; new module `_lib/pinned_constraints.py`)* |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2378:+| v2.58 | PLAN-182 W1 (SENT-S319 pack, 2026-08-21) — 1 NEW metadata-only action `salt_rotation_registered` (the ONE sanctioned salt-rotation register of the ADR-079 S318 amendment §2: per-project `.salt` minting becomes observable in the HMAC chain — the amendment's cure for the silent mint-and-persist the W0 measured in `injection_salt.py`). Via LAZY `emit_generic` from `_lib/injection_salt.py::_register_mint` into a dedicated deny-by-default `_SALT_ROTATION_REGISTERED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch: `reason` closed-enum coerced to `other`, `salt_scope` fixed to `project`, `slug_sha256` 16-hex prefix shape-checked to `"invalid"`. The slug text (as a payload value) and the salt bytes never reach the wire; the baseline `project` field carries the repository path, as on every registered action. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 326 -> 327. HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(1 new per-action allowlist `_SALT_ROTATION_REGISTERED_ALLOWLIST` + closed enum `_SALT_ROTATION_REASONS` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2379:+| v2.59 | PLAN-179 W2 + W4 (staged-w24 pack, ADR-195 work-boundary persistence; Owner decision 2026-08-25 "3 actions — registra ledger_entry_rejected") — 3 NEW metadata-only actions. `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` + `ledger_checkpoint_skipped`: the ADVISORY work-boundary rail (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash) makes an OMITTED plan checkpoint visible at the one boundary this repo already has — a commit — instead of at session death, which S309 proved does not arrive. The two are separate actions so the measure-first window has a denominator. `ledger_entry_rejected`: the W4 ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), which used to borrow `prompt_injection_detected` for `reason="scanner_hit"` and go breadcrumb-only for the other four reasons; that fallback rung is REMOVED with this registration, because filing an infrastructure discard as a DETECTION poisons the FPR series the window measures. All three route through dedicated deny-by-default `_scrub_*` branches (`_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`), NONE is in `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`, and every integer field is TYPE-strict (`bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, `float` -> `0`, never rounded — S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). The commit message, the committed paths, the ledger content and the rejected entry body have no allowed field name at all. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327 -> 330. ONE new typed emitter (`emit_ledger_entry_rejected`). HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(3 new per-action allowlists + closed enums `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_OUTCOMES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIP_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SCOPE_SOURCES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_STATE_KINDS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_DECISIONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` + the TYPE-strict clamp `_ledger_int_field` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2380:+| v2.60 | PLAN-179 W2 US7+US8 + US2b-valve (wave-179-close ceremony; Owner ratification 2026-08-31 "Fechar tudo") — 1 NEW metadata-only action `session_memory_delta_observed` (SessionEnd stat-only memory-delta observation; `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 330 -> 331, golden registry regenerated in the same patch). NO change to any existing action, and that is load-bearing: US7's ledger INDEX rides INSIDE the PreCompact snapshot blob (`ledger_index` — plan id derived from commit PATHS, never `resolve_plan_id`, emenda r1-C6) and the PostCompact half renders only the structural path+short-sha pair, so `compaction_continuity_snapshot` / `compaction_context_reinjected` keep their existing field sets and `pointer_count` keeps counting POINTERS ONLY — one more pointer within the existing 0..9 clamp is not a semantic re-scope, and the ledger section TITLES reach neither the wire nor the post-compaction instruction stream (Codex R5 P1-1 class). The US2b valve is stderr-breadcrumb-only: integer-permille η from the MEASURED `F+S=112638` / `T=998043` (w0-measurement.md §C/§E) — raw counts stay in the operator channel, the correct home the v2.56 row already established; "deny" is documented as a substrate limit (PreCompact has no deny channel), never claimed as hook behaviour. | *(1 new per-action allowlist `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` + closed sets `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OUTCOMES` / `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_ANCHOR_SOURCES` + typed wrapper `emit_session_memory_delta_observed` in `audit_emit.py`)* |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/transcript-rc1-4.log:2871:SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:591:| v2.60 | PLAN-179 W2 US7+US8 + US2b-valve (wave-179-close ceremony; Owner ratification 2026-08-31 "Fechar tudo") — 1 NEW metadata-only action `session_memory_delta_observed` (SessionEnd stat-only memory-delta observation; `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 330 -> 331, golden registry regenerated in the same patch). NO change to any existing action, and that is load-bearing: US7's ledger INDEX rides INSIDE the PreCompact snapshot blob (`ledger_index` — plan id derived from commit PATHS, never `resolve_plan_id`, emenda r1-C6) and the PostCompact half renders only the structural path+short-sha pair, so `compaction_continuity_snapshot` / `compaction_context_reinjected` keep their existing field sets and `pointer_count` keeps counting POINTERS ONLY — one more pointer within the existing 0..9 clamp is not a semantic re-scope, and the ledger section TITLES reach neither the wire nor the post-compaction instruction stream (Codex R5 P1-1 class). The US2b valve is stderr-breadcrumb-only: integer-permille η from the MEASURED `F+S=112638` / `T=998043` (w0-measurement.md §C/§E) — raw counts stay in the operator channel, the correct home the v2.56 row already established; "deny" is documented as a substrate limit (PreCompact has no deny channel), never claimed as hook behaviour. | *(1 new per-action allowlist `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` + closed sets `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OUTCOMES` / `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_ANCHOR_SOURCES` + typed wrapper `emit_session_memory_delta_observed` in `audit_emit.py`)* |
