override), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget this invocation ran under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Purpose is §4(i): before this field a case F produced by a sub-floor `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S` export was byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage, which made the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented kill-switch. Encoding is load-bearing, not stylistic: a float in an HMAC-covered field is rejected by `_lib/canonical_json.py` and the spool writer then DROPS THE WHOLE EVENT with only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — for this action that would manufacture the very /ceo-boot liveness deficit `review_id` exists to disprove), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline HMAC-chain invariant. PLAN-081 Phase 3 (S100 ceremony 2026-05-10) — emitted by `.claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:_decide_with_matrix()` once per Pair-Rail PreToolUse evaluation that reaches the matrix arm (write tool + L3+ path + no sentinel bypass). Source action for `fp_rate_30d` and `disagreement_rate_30d` predicate aggregators. ADR-107 + ADR-108 ACCEPTED gate. Sec MF-3 invariant: NEVER persist raw Codex review body / proposed-content / file path. Registered with `KERNEL_OVERRIDE` bypass since `audit_emit.py` is in `_KERNEL_PATHS`. |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:379:| `tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed` (v2.34) | `action`, `reason_code` (str — closed enum: `advisory_safety_net` / `bad_mode` / `depth_limit` / `key_count` / `missing` / `not_object` / `open_failed` / `oversize` / `parse_error` / `read_failed` / `schema_mismatch` / `stat_error` / `type_mismatch` / `unknown_model`), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`. PLAN-116 (S172 2026-05-27) — tier-policy loader advisory-only fallback telemetry. Replaces the PLAN-093 Wave C.3 `tier_policy_misrouting_advised` piggyback (which dropped a free-text `reason` field on every emit → audit-log.errors noise). NO ATLAS technique (loader telemetry, not a detection signal — distinct from `tier_policy_misrouting_advised`'s AML.T0048). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:494:| `codex_review_verdict` (v2.52) | `action`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `clean` / `findings` / `skipped_failopen` / `detected_only`; an unrecognized value is COERCED to `skipped_failopen` — never to a healthy-class value, so unparseable telemetry input can never claim rail health), `diff_sha256` (str — 64-lowercase-hex sha256 of the reviewed assembled risky diff, shape-validated; any off-shape value COERCED to `""`), `session_id` (threaded from the Stop-hook stdin event, fallback `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env, then `""`), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — Stop-hook cross-model review OUTCOME, emitted by `codex_review_user_code.py` once per distinct (`diff_sha256`, `outcome`) pair (telemetry dedupe SEPARATE from the review-status dedupe, so Stop-retry loops re-review without re-emitting). `clean`/`findings` require a strictly PARSED verdict (bounded `- <file>: <issue>` grammar or exact `CLEAN`); infra fail-open (codex missing / rc!=0 / empty stdout / timeout) AND malformed output both map to `skipped_failopen`; DETECT-ONLY default mode maps its nudge to `detected_only` (neutral). Feeds the /ceo-boot `failopen_rail_liveness_7d` `stop_review` sub-rail. Typed emitter `emit_codex_review_verdict`; dedicated deny-by-default `_CODEX_REVIEW_VERDICT_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the verdict TEXT, the diff content, file paths (a Codex finding can quote secrets from the reviewed diff). Deliberately NOT `pair_rail_codex_unavailable` — that action feeds the dispatcher's Codex-outage predicate and must stay unpolluted. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:495:| `pair_rail_review_expected` (v2.52) | `action`, `tool_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`; off-enum COERCED to `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path, the SAME token/helper as `pair_rail_case`; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to empty; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard; r4 F2, retained as the LEGACY fallback bucket key + harmless secondary key — id-less events still pair per (session, file-hash) BUCKET), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty; r6 F2: raw value validated, off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to empty — never truncated); r5 F2 — THE invocation correlation key: minted per review entry by `_decide()` (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`, so the /ceo-boot deficit pairs a specific expected with its OWN case — counting (even (session, file-hash)-bucketed) cannot: an old completed case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1. An EXPECTED `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window = an outstanding (dead) review -> RED; off-shape COERCED to empty; empty falls back to the bucket-count heuristic (best-effort, pre-land events only — post-land every review carries an id)), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the paired review runs under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Carried on the DENOMINATOR as well as the case so the pair records the budget it ran under even when the case never arrives — see the `pair_rail_case` row for the §4(i) rationale and for why the integer encoding is load-bearing), `session_id` (explicit required kwarg on the typed emitter — the hook threads the PreToolUse event's own session id, no silent default), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — canonical-edit review ENTERED marker, emitted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` only after the kill-switch / non-write-tool / not-L3+ / sentinel-bypass arms have all returned (those paths emit NOTHING). The durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail` activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and escalates RED; zero expected + zero outcomes is vacuously green; a healthy outcome from session B never masks session A. Typed emitter `emit_pair_rail_review_expected`; dedicated deny-by-default `_PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: file paths, proposed content, any review text. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:504:| `ledger_entry_rejected` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `signal` (str — fixed vocabulary of ONE: `ledger_write_gate`; this action has exactly one producer, so any other value names a caller that is not the gate and is COERCED), `decision` (str — CLOSED enum: `accept` / `reject`; an unreadable value COERCES to `reject`, FAIL-CLOSED, because an unreadable security verdict is a rejection and never an acceptance), `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `not_scanned_trusted_provenance` / `scanner_hit` / `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input`; off-enum COERCES to `malformed_input`, also fail-CLOSED), `family` (str — CLOSED enum, the UNION of the gate's own local families {`none`, `scanner_unavailable`, `oversize`, `malformed_input`, `unknown_family`} and the pattern CATALOGUE `_lib/injection_patterns.family_names()` {`directive_prose`, `harness_mimicry`, `provider_tokens`, `role_preamble`}; off-enum COERCED to `unknown_family`. Deliberately STRICTER than `prompt_injection_detected`, whose branch allowlists `family` by NAME but leaves its VALUE caller-chosen), `hits_count` (int 0..9999 — clamped), `bytes_scanned` (int 0..8192 — clamped at the gate's `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES`; an oversize body is rejected WITHOUT scanning, so this ceiling can never truncate a legitimate value), `scanned` (int 0/1), `enforced` (int 0/1 — whether the fail-CLOSED verdict BINDS in the current posture; kept separate from `decision` so an advisory-window row records what enforcement WOULD have done without pretending it happened), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W4 / ADR-195 — the ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), registered by Owner decision 2026-08-25 ("3 actions"). It exists precisely so a discard is NOT filed as `prompt_injection_detected`: routing `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input` into a DETECTION action would poison the very false-positive series the advisory window has to measure. There is deliberately NO fallback action — a missing or raising emitter degrades to a LOUD breadcrumb and `audit_channel="unavailable"`, never to a quieter series. Typed emitter `emit_ledger_entry_rejected` (keywords mirror `GateVerdict.to_audit_fields()` exactly). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the rejected entry BODY (not even a truncated preview — public repo, LLM06), the entry id, and any path. NO ATLAS technique (the DETECTION that may underlie a `scanner_hit` is `prompt_injection_detected`'s job; this row is the gate's disposal record). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:530:| `compaction_continuity_snapshot` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `trigger` (str — CLOSED enum: `manual` / `auto` / `other`; coerced to `other`), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape, else `unknown`), `chain_length` (int — clamped 0..99999999), `snapshot_outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `written` / `written_session_scope` / `scratchpad_unavailable` / `error` / `other`; coerced to `other`; `written_session_scope` added v2.56 / PLAN-179 W1 US3 — the snapshot WAS written, but to the SESSION-scoped fallback location because `resolve_plan_id()` could not name a plan. That is the S309 fires-proof DOMINANT path, not an edge: a `plan_transition` is emitted only on a status CHANGE, so a long session — exactly the kind that compacts — normally carries none of its own (S309 census: 2 events in 12,515 audit lines). Kept DISTINCT from `written` so a ledger can separate plan-scoped from session-scoped continuity instead of conflating the two; the enum stays CLOSED and anything else still coerces to `other`), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H1 (anthropic-surface-harvest; ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PreCompact governance snapshot: before the harness compacts a long session (manual `/compact` or auto context-window threshold), `check_precompact_continuity.py` snapshotted plan-id + execution-unit position + pending-ceremony flags to the plan-scoped scratchpad + read the audit HMAC-chain anchor (last-hmac prefix + chain-length). ONE emit per compaction event. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_precompact_continuity.py` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — `settings_tamper_detected` precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY_SNAPSHOT_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the snapshot BODY — the plan path text, the execution-unit checkbox label, the ceremony script paths, the full last-hmac hex (the snapshot lives in the plan-scoped, secrets-redacted scratchpad; the wire carries closed enums + the chain_length counter only). Honest coverage boundary: ADR-153 §H2 (a hook is disarmed by `disableAllHooks`; S3 boot tripwires + W5 O10 OTEL witness are the named compensators). NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:531:| `compaction_context_reinjected` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape, else `unknown`), `snapshot_found` (bool — coerced to `false`), `snapshot_age_s` (int — clamped 0..9999999), `pointer_count` (int — clamped 0..9; POINTERS ONLY. Its meaning is UNCHANGED by PLAN-179, deliberately: a counter that is silently re-scoped makes its own historical series uncomparable, so the constraint block below got a NEW counter instead of a widened one. A consumer may compare `pointer_count` across the whole v2.43+ series), `constraint_count` (int — v2.56 / PLAN-179 W1-b, amendment r1-C3: the count of PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINTS re-stated verbatim after compaction, sourced from `_lib/pinned_constraints.constraint_count()` — the SET size, never the rendered LINE count, because the block carries a header line and a counter that drifts with formatting is not a counter. Constraints and pointers hold SEPARATE budgets: the 9-line pointer cap can never truncate a governance rule. Treatment in the scrub branch: `max(0, min(99, int(...)))` with the same `except (TypeError, ValueError) -> 0` fallback the sibling counters use. **STATUS — both halves land in THIS ceremony (PLAN-179 W0/W1):** `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch carries the clamp above, so the deny-by-default scrub KEEPS the field and `check_postcompact_reinject.py` puts a real clamped `int` on the wire. A consumer MUST still read an ABSENT `constraint_count` as “this producer predates constraint pinning”, NEVER as “zero constraints pinned” — absence and zero are different facts, and `constraint_count=0` is itself meaningful (it is what `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0` produces)), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H1 (anthropic-surface-harvest; ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PostCompact governance reinjection: after compaction, `check_postcompact_reinject.py` read the PreCompact snapshot from the plan scratchpad and reinjected governance POINTERS (active PLAN, execution-unit position, Gate-1 re-read reminder, pending ceremonies, HMAC anchor) via `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. POINTERS ONLY — never file CONTENTS (the Option-A prompt-injection surface, ADR-153 §Decision). ONE emit per PostCompact event. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the reinjected pointer TEXT, the plan path/label, the ceremony paths, the scratchpad body (only the closed enums + counters persist). PLAN-179 W1-b [r1-C3] prepends a PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT block AHEAD of the pointers: a pointer is not a restriction — ADR-153's pointers say WHERE the rules live, the pinned block re-states the rules THEMSELVES from a CODE constant (`_lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS`), never from disk, so the prompt-injection reasoning that forces POINTERS-ONLY on the snapshot simply does not apply to it. The constraint TEXT is no more on the wire than the pointer text — only `constraint_count` is. Dedicated kill-switch `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0`, deliberately SEPARATE from `CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`: an operator disarming the continuity SNAPSHOT must not silently disarm the governance floor. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:587:| v2.56 | PLAN-179 W0 US2 + W1 US3 + W1-b (context-continuity successor rail / ADR-153, debate amendments 8.1 + r1-C3, 2026-08-18) — 1 NEW metadata-only action `context_pressure_observed` (EDGE-TRIGGERED: emitted only on a percent-rung TRANSITION, gated by `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(...)` against the `context-pressure-last-bucket` marker under the gitignored `.claude/state/` — per-session when the producer supplies a session id (`<basename>.<sanitized-id>`), falling back to the bare project-wide basename otherwise, a documented degraded mode in which two concurrent sessions in one repo can interfere with each other's hysteresis; hysteresis, never sampling — a per-turn sampler would append one row per prompt while the session sits in one rung), PLUS 1 additive value on the EXISTING closed `snapshot_outcome` enum of `compaction_continuity_snapshot` — `written_session_scope`, the S309 fires-proof DOMINANT path where the snapshot lands in the session-scoped fallback because `resolve_plan_id()` could not name a plan — PLUS 1 NEW bounded field `constraint_count` on the EXISTING `compaction_context_reinjected` action. NO new typed emitter: `context_pressure_observed` goes through `emit_generic` (compaction-pair / `settings_tamper_detected` precedent) into a dedicated deny-by-default `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`; `plan_id` reuses the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator. **`used_bucket`'s integer typing is normative, not stylistic:** `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict (rejects `bool`, an `int` subclass, and rejects `float` — `40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python, so a plain membership test would wave a float onto the wire and `_lib/canonical_json.py` would then drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb; same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`). Off-set values coerce to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the `{40,60,80,90,95}` enum. **`pointer_count` is UNCHANGED** and keeps counting POINTERS ONLY — constraint pinning landed as the SEPARATE `constraint_count` rather than by re-defining what `pointer_count` measures, because a silently re-scoped counter makes its historical series uncomparable (amendment r1-C3 is what makes this SPEC bump non-optional). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. Registered via the PLAN-179 W0/W1 pack ceremony (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 324 -> 325; the staged set literal measures 325). **CODE/ROW PARITY — three integration gaps were found by the W0/W1 cross-file pass and are CLOSED by this same ceremony, so this row describes the wire as shipped, not as intended:** (1) `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch clamps it `max(0, min(99, int(...)))`, so the deny-by-default scrub keeps it; (2) the shipped producer of `context_pressure_observed` (`check_precompact_continuity.py:_progress_guard`) probes `getattr(audit_emit, "should_emit_context_pressure", None)` — the name that actually exists — and calls it with the crossed bucket, `state_dir = <project>/.claude/state` and the trusted session id, retrying the two-argument shape on `TypeError` so an adopter whose `audit_emit` predates per-session markers degrades to the project-wide marker instead of losing the observation; an earlier draft probed `edge_trigger_should_emit`, a name in neither library, which suppressed every emit; (3) that producer now sends the allowlisted trio `used_bucket` / `event_source` / `plan_id`, where `used_bucket` is the PERCENT rung from `_context_used_pct` + `_pressure_bucket` and the rung SET is DERIVED from `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` at call time rather than restated ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]); the earlier `used_tokens_bucket` (`used_tokens // 10000`) and `floor_tokens` are gone from the wire and survive only in the operator's stderr breadcrumb, which is the correct home for a raw count. A conformance test asserting this row against the wire is expected to pass. **Producer coverage is still partial and that is not a defect of this row:** `precompact` is the only `event_source` with a shipped producer; `sessionstart_compact` and `userpromptsubmit` remain RESERVED, and their absence means “no producer yet”, never “no pressure observed on that channel”. | *(1 additive value on the existing `_COMPACTION_SNAPSHOT_OUTCOMES` closed enum; 1 additive field on `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`; 1 new per-action allowlist `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` + closed sets `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` / `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCES` + type-strict validator `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` + edge-trigger helper `should_emit_context_pressure` and marker basename `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_STATE_BASENAME` in `audit_emit.py`; new module `_lib/pinned_constraints.py`)* |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:590:| v2.59 | PLAN-179 W2 + W4 (staged-w24 pack, ADR-195 work-boundary persistence; Owner decision 2026-08-25 "3 actions — registra ledger_entry_rejected") — 3 NEW metadata-only actions. `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` + `ledger_checkpoint_skipped`: the ADVISORY work-boundary rail (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash) makes an OMITTED plan checkpoint visible at the one boundary this repo already has — a commit — instead of at session death, which S309 proved does not arrive. The two are separate actions so the measure-first window has a denominator. `ledger_entry_rejected`: the W4 ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), which used to borrow `prompt_injection_detected` for `reason="scanner_hit"` and go breadcrumb-only for the other four reasons; that fallback rung is REMOVED with this registration, because filing an infrastructure discard as a DETECTION poisons the FPR series the window measures. All three route through dedicated deny-by-default `_scrub_*` branches (`_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`), NONE is in `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`, and every integer field is TYPE-strict (`bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, `float` -> `0`, never rounded — S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). The commit message, the committed paths, the ledger content and the rejected entry body have no allowed field name at all. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327 -> 330. ONE new typed emitter (`emit_ledger_entry_rejected`). HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(3 new per-action allowlists + closed enums `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_OUTCOMES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIP_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SCOPE_SOURCES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_STATE_KINDS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_DECISIONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` + the TYPE-strict clamp `_ledger_int_field` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
